ntationMode":"auto-scored","activityType":"normalized_students_book","questions":[{"number":1,"prompt":"The famous musician has worked on hundreds of ____ during his career.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["soundtracks"],"options":["scripts","soundtracks","plots","special effects"]},{"number":2,"prompt":"The concert hall was full and they had to ____ dozens of people last night.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["turn away"],"options":["turn around","turn down","turn to","turn away"]},{"number":3,"prompt":"As soon as I saw the opening ____, I knew that I was going to love the film.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["scene"],"options":["scene","episode","rehearsal","season"]},{"number":4,"prompt":"The young actress hasn’t been offered any leading ____ yet, but she has appeared in a number of plays.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["roles"],"options":["reviews","genres","roles","performances"]},{"number":5,"prompt":"They weren’t really looking forward to the show, but it ____ to be very entertaining.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["turned out"],"options":["turned down","turned into","turned out","turned up"]},{"number":6,"prompt":"They had to stop filming because the ____ had run out of money.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["producer"],"options":["designer","producer","cast","crew"]},{"number":7,"prompt":"To our great ____, we couldn’t get tickets for the show.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["disappointment"],"options":["stimulation","confusion","disappointment","amusement"]},{"number":8,"prompt":"The director was delighted with the actor’s ____ performance.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["inspired"],"options":["inspired","frustrated","entertained","frightened"]},{"number":9,"prompt":"British bands ____ the show at this year’s music awards.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["stole"],"options":["broke","stole","followed","set"]},{"number":10,"prompt":"There are far fewer ____ than there used to be due to streaming services like Netflix.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["cinemagoers"],"options":["box-offices","binge-watching","sub-plots","cinemagoers"]}]},{"stableNormalizedId":"ultimate-b2-sb-u1-p8-o2","partNumber":8,"printedPage":16,"title":"Review 1 · Grammar","instructions":"Choose the correct answers.","implementationMode":"auto-scored","activityType":"normalized_students_book","questions":[{"number":1,"prompt":"Be quiet, please! The director ____ the actors instructions for the next scene.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["is giving"],"options":["gives","is giving","has given","has been giving"]},{"number":2,"prompt":"We ____ to the theatre in London’s West End a few times this year.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["have been"],"options":["have been","have gone","are going","are being"]},{"number":3,"prompt":"The leading actor ____ about something! I wish he would stop!","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["is always complaining"],"options":["has always been complaining","always complaining","is always complaining","has always complained"]},{"number":4,"prompt":"What ____ of Brad Pitt’s new film?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["do you think"],"options":["do you think","you are thinking","have you thought","are you thinking"]},{"number":5,"prompt":"This is the first time ____ this programme. It’s good, isn’t it?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["I’ve watched"],"options":["I watch","I’m watching","I’ve been watching","I’ve watched"]},{"number":6,"prompt":"Do you know what time ____?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["the market opens"],"options":["does the market open","the market opens","the market is open","is the market opening"]},{"number":7,"prompt":"My dad ____ as a film director. He used to be a set designer.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["hasn’t always worked"],"options":["isn’t always working","doesn’t always work","hasn’t always worked","hasn’t always been working"]},{"number":8,"prompt":"I ____ at the local theatre at the moment, and I love it!","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["am working"],"options":["am working","work","have worked","have been working"]},{"number":9,"prompt":"We’re exhausted because we ____ for hours.","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["have been rehearsing"],"options":["are rehearsing","have rehearsed","rehearse","have been rehearsing"]},{"number":10,"prompt":"My friend ____ acting lessons for a while now, and she has an audition next week!","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["has been taking"],"options":["takes","is taking","has been taking","has been taken"]}]},{"stableNormalizedId":"ultimate-b2-sb-u1-p9-o1","partNumber":9,"printedPage":17,"title":"B2 Practice 1 · Exercise 1","instructions":"You are going to read an article about watching TV series. For questions 1–6, choose the answer (A, B, C or D) which you think fits best according to the text.","implementationMode":"auto-scored","activityType":"normalized_students_book","questions":[{"number":1,"prompt":"At the end of the first paragraph, the writer is emphasising","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["how long some people might binge-watch for."],"options":["how long some people might binge-watch for.","that viewers’ habits have not changed.","how unhealthy some people’s viewing habits are.","that some series can become boring."]},{"number":2,"prompt":"What was the purpose of the study mentioned in the second paragraph?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["to determine the habits of binge-watchers"],"options":["to identify the most popular horror shows","to find out which age group watched thrillers and horror shows","to determine the habits of binge-watchers","to understand why people stayed up all night"]},{"number":3,"prompt":"What particularly impressed the writer about The Umbrella Academy?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["the music"],"options":["its main characters","the plot","its popularity","the music"]},{"number":4,"prompt":"Why does the writer mention covering your eyes in IT?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["because viewers might be scared by what they see"],"options":["because viewers might be scared by what they see","because viewers will not understand what is happening","because parts of the series are slow-moving and tiring","because information about the next episode is revealed"]},{"number":5,"prompt":"According to the text, which series’ themes have been modernised?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["Anne with an E"],"options":["The Umbrella Academy","Stranger Things","Anne with an E","The Letter for the King"]},{"number":6,"prompt":"What is the writer’s main point in the last paragraph?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["Binge-watching and devouring a book are similar behaviours."],"options":["As a society, we watch too much TV.","We need to encourage people to read more.","Binge-watching and devouring a book are similar behaviours.","Once viewers start binge-watching, they cannot stop."]}]},{"stableNormalizedId":"ultimate-b2-sb-u1-p10-o1","partNumber":10,"printedPage":18,"title":"B2 Practice 1 · Exercise 2","instructions":"You will hear people talking in eight different situations. For questions 1–8, choose the best answer (A, B or C).","implementationMode":"auto-scored","activityType":"normalized_students_book","questions":[{"number":1,"prompt":"You hear an announcement in a theatre. What is the announcer’s main purpose?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["to prepare the audience for the start of the play"],"options":["to prepare the audience for the start of the play","to describe the play","to explain where the audience should sit"]},{"number":2,"prompt":"You hear a teacher talking to his class. What does he want the students to do?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["write about each character’s personality"],"options":["read the next chapter of their book","write about each character’s personality","re-read the essays they have written"]},{"number":3,"prompt":"You hear a review on the radio describing a musical. What has changed since he saw it?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["They have replaced a cast member."],"options":["They have replaced a cast member.","Child actors play all the parts.","The children’s singing has improved."]},{"number":4,"prompt":"You hear part of a news programme. What has happened north of Oldfield?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["Road traffic has been blocked."],"options":["The weather has changed suddenly.","Lorry drivers have been causing long delays.","Road traffic has been blocked."]},{"number":5,"prompt":"You hear a boy leaving a message for his friend. Why is he calling?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["to invite him somewhere"],"options":["to congratulate him","to offer tips on studying","to invite him somewhere"]},{"number":6,"prompt":"You hear a woman talking to her son about food. What is she doing?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["giving him a choice of what to eat now"],"options":["complaining about the boy’s eating habits","giving him a choice of what to eat now","asking the boy to help in preparing the meals"]},{"number":7,"prompt":"You hear a girl talking about her school project. What does she say about the app she uses?","questionType":"multiple_choice","acceptedAnswers":["It is for keeping a record of the birds they have seen."],"options":["It is for keeping a record of the birds they have seen.","It helps you make videos of the birds you see.","It is useful for writing descriptions of birds."]},{"number":8,"prompt":"You hear t